THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
----------------------

This product includes third-party software. Each component remains under its
own licence; the terms in LICENSE.md apply to this product, not to them.

The authoritative, complete inventory is the dependency manifests in this
repository: go.mod / go.sum for the Go modules, and package.json /
package-lock.json for the npm packages. Those are generated and stay current;
this file records only the points that need a stated position.

The Go and npm dependency trees were audited before publication and contain no
strong or network copyleft components: no GPL, AGPL, LGPL, SSPL, CDDL, EPL, BUSL
or Elastic-licensed code is present. The Go dependencies are MIT, Apache-2.0 and
BSD, except for the one MPL-2.0 module listed below; the npm dependencies are
predominantly MIT and ISC. The one file-level copyleft licence present is
MPL-2.0 — see the MPL-2.0 section below, which lists every MPL component.


Dual-licensed components — our election
---------------------------------------

jszip is offered by its authors under either the MIT licence or GPL-3.0-or-later.
We take it under the MIT licence.

Recording this matters: silence about which arm of a dual licence was taken is
what creates an argument years later.


Mozilla Public License 2.0 components
-------------------------------------

MPL-2.0 is a file-level copyleft: it obliges publication of modifications to
MPL-licensed files. We do not modify them. MPL-2.0 components are accepted in
this product, build-time or runtime, on that basis and on the condition that each
one is listed in this section — so this list is the complete set, and a component
absent from it is a component we do not ship.

- lightningcss (and its platform-specific binaries) — build-time tooling, not
  distributed in the product.
- github.com/go-sql-driver/mysql — the MySQL client used by database
  interrogation. Linked, unmodified, into the device-interrogation-service and
  the Interrogation Agent binaries. Its source is available at
  https://github.com/go-sql-driver/mysql.

Their notices are retained.


THIRD-PARTY DATA
----------------

This product mirrors third-party datasets into your own deployment, and can
export them as an offline bundle for an air-gapped install. Each source keeps its
own terms, and those terms travel with the data — a built bundle carries this
same wording as an ATTRIBUTION.md file inside it.

- NVD (NIST). This product uses data from the NVD API but is not endorsed or
  certified by the NVD. See https://nvd.nist.gov/developers/terms-of-use.
- OSV (osv.dev). The aggregated database is published under CC-BY-4.0.
  Attribution: OSV, https://osv.dev, and the upstream database named on each
  record. See https://github.com/google/osv.dev.
- endoflife.date. A community-maintained dataset, mirrored under its published
  API terms. See https://endoflife.date/docs/api.


THIRD-PARTY TEST FIXTURES
-------------------------

Some automated tests in this repository run against real, captured network
device command output redistributed from a third-party project under a
compatible licence, rather than hand-written sample text. This is test-only
content — it never ships in a built image or the Helm chart — but it is
git-tracked, so it is part of what this repository publishes.

- networktocode/ntc-templates (https://github.com/networktocode/ntc-templates),
  licensed Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2015 Jason Edelman / Network to Code,
  LLC. Real Cisco IOS, IOS-XE, NX-OS, IOS-XR and ASA `show` command output from
  its `tests/` directory was sanitised (addresses rewritten to RFC 5737/3849
  documentation ranges, serial numbers and any credential-shaped text redacted)
  and copied into `shared/deviceinterrogation/testdata/real/`. See the
  `PROVENANCE.md` file in each vendor subdirectory there for the exact source
  commit, original path and per-file notes.


